WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.049 --> 00:00:03.690
Did you know that the world is ruled by one
company?

00:00:03.690 --> 00:00:07.470
Taiwan Semiconductor Manufacturing Company
may not be a household name.

00:00:07.470 --> 00:00:10.360
But its chips are everywhere.

00:00:10.360 --> 00:00:17.419
In iPhones, air conditioning units, smart
doorbells, computers, cars, F-35 fighter jets,

00:00:17.419 --> 00:00:21.289
and even NASA’s Perseverance Rover that
landed on Mars.

00:00:21.289 --> 00:00:25.859
The reason automakers haven’t been making
enough cars is because of a shortage of these

00:00:25.859 --> 00:00:29.880
sophisticated chips that power functions like
braking.

00:00:29.880 --> 00:00:33.480
Semiconductor chips are the new “oil”
in terms of our dependence on them.

00:00:33.480 --> 00:00:36.640
One company pretty much has a global monopoly.

00:00:36.640 --> 00:00:43.429
Nestled on the northwest coast of Taiwan,
TSMC produces 92% of the most advanced chips

00:00:43.429 --> 00:00:44.429
in the world.

00:00:44.429 --> 00:00:49.130
It’s one of only two companies that mass
produces chips below 10 nanometers, the other

00:00:49.130 --> 00:00:50.410
being Samsung.

00:00:50.410 --> 00:00:56.180
Nanometer refers to the length of a transistor
- TINY switches 10,000 times thinner than

00:00:56.180 --> 00:00:59.160
a human hair that control electric currents.

00:00:59.160 --> 00:01:03.140
One nanometer is equal to one billionth of
a meter.

00:01:03.140 --> 00:01:06.730
The smaller the transistor, the more that
can be crammed together.

00:01:06.730 --> 00:01:10.900
The more transistors you have, the better
the chip, and the more powerful your computer

00:01:10.900 --> 00:01:11.900
will be.

00:01:11.900 --> 00:01:17.690
When House Speaker Nancy Pelosi visited Taiwan
in August 2022, she made it a point to meet

00:01:17.690 --> 00:01:22.680
with TSMC Chairman Mark Liu - a sign of just
how important the company is.

00:01:22.680 --> 00:01:27.890
Beijing spent weeks telling Pelosi not to
go to Taiwan, an island that Chinese President

00:01:27.890 --> 00:01:32.510
Xi Jinping believes is a breakaway province
and has threatened to invade.

00:01:32.510 --> 00:01:37.910
In light of Pelosi’s visit, Beijing sanctioned
Taiwan by suspending imports of citrus fruits

00:01:37.910 --> 00:01:39.060
and fish.

00:01:39.060 --> 00:01:46.250
Of course, Beijing did NOT ban Taiwanese semiconductors
because it relies on them like everyone else.

00:01:46.250 --> 00:01:50.150
Semiconductors have become a key part of the
tech rivalry between the U.S. and China.

00:01:50.150 --> 00:01:55.030
There are concerns that an invasion of Taiwan
by China could choke off the supply of these

00:01:55.030 --> 00:01:59.840
cutting-edge chips to the rest of the world
and give Beijing control of this essential

00:01:59.840 --> 00:02:00.890
technology.

00:02:00.890 --> 00:02:05.860
So, how did Taiwan Semiconductor become so
dominant?

00:02:05.860 --> 00:02:11.099
The fundamental technology was actually invented
in America and gave Silicon Valley its name

00:02:11.099 --> 00:02:13.890
- as most chips are created with silicon.

00:02:13.890 --> 00:02:17.770
In the nineties, the U.S. manufactured a third
of the world’s chips.

00:02:17.770 --> 00:02:18.770
Today?

00:02:18.770 --> 00:02:22.190
None of the advanced chips is made in the
USA.

00:02:22.190 --> 00:02:24.590
Companies like Intel used to build and design
chips in-house.

00:02:24.590 --> 00:02:29.940
But beginning in the 1980s, American firms
started to struggle against competition from

00:02:29.940 --> 00:02:33.850
Japanese companies, so they outsourced some
parts of their business that were draining

00:02:33.850 --> 00:02:39.000
their profits, including the expensive factories
that produce semiconductor chips.

00:02:39.000 --> 00:02:42.140
Morris Chang noticed this trend and took advantage
of it.

00:02:42.140 --> 00:02:46.490
He was born in China and in 1949, he moved
to the States where he eventually earned a

00:02:46.490 --> 00:02:49.660
Ph.D. in electrical engineering from Stanford.

00:02:49.660 --> 00:02:54.069
He spent 25 years rising through the ranks
of Texas Instruments before the Taiwanese

00:02:54.069 --> 00:02:58.440
government offered him a chance to develop
its semiconductor industry.

00:02:58.440 --> 00:03:03.330
Chang realized that there was a great opportunity
to create a new company focused solely on

00:03:03.330 --> 00:03:07.080
making chips that could supply all needs.

00:03:07.080 --> 00:03:09.880
In 1987, TSMC was born.

00:03:09.880 --> 00:03:14.540
Chang initially priced the chips at a loss
to capture a larger market share in the hopes

00:03:14.540 --> 00:03:18.319
that costs would eventually be reduced enough
to generate a profit.

00:03:18.319 --> 00:03:20.880
His strategy paid off, big time.

00:03:20.880 --> 00:03:25.870
The world’s largest tech companies all rely
on TSMC: Apple, Intel, Qualcomm, AMD, Nvidia,

00:03:25.870 --> 00:03:32.070
Chinese tech giant Huawei, and Tesla.

00:03:32.070 --> 00:03:36.940
Manufacturing semiconductor chips that are
the size of a fingernail is crazy difficult.

00:03:36.940 --> 00:03:42.270
Each tiny chip is packed with as many as 50
billion transistors.

00:03:42.270 --> 00:03:47.250
The process begins by cutting silicon wafers
- thin slices of semiconductors that kind

00:03:47.250 --> 00:03:50.770
of look like shiny mirrors - into individual
chips.

00:03:50.770 --> 00:03:53.800
Employees must wear protective gear when handling
them.

00:03:53.800 --> 00:03:59.790
If even a speck of dust falls onto a wafer,
the entire batch risks being ruined.

00:03:59.790 --> 00:04:04.739
The chips are made by etching tiny patterns
across the wafer, layer upon layer.

00:04:04.739 --> 00:04:08.459
To create the layers, the wafer is coated
with a light-sensitive chemical.

00:04:08.459 --> 00:04:14.300
It’s kind of like layering a cake, except
in this case the cake has 75 layers and takes

00:04:14.300 --> 00:04:15.910
three months to make.

00:04:15.910 --> 00:04:19.979
The layers are connected by copper wires that
carry electrical power.

00:04:19.979 --> 00:04:25.020
The entire process is daunting and TSMC has
the undisputed edge.

00:04:25.020 --> 00:04:29.319
But things are getting complicated as it finds
itself caught in the middle of a tug of war

00:04:29.319 --> 00:04:31.300
between the two superpowers.

00:04:31.300 --> 00:04:35.949
In August, President Biden signed the CHIPS
Act into law which bans companies that receive

00:04:35.949 --> 00:04:43.169
American subsidies from manufacturing sophisticated
chips for China, any that are below 28 nanometers.

00:04:43.169 --> 00:04:49.860
Washington is offering $52 billion in subsidies
to encourage manufacturers like TSMC to build

00:04:49.860 --> 00:04:51.860
semiconductors plants in the U.S.

00:04:51.860 --> 00:04:57.520
One is scheduled to open in Arizona in 2024,
which TSMC previewed on its LinkedIn page.

00:04:57.520 --> 00:05:01.940
But it will still represent only a small sliver
of global chip production.

00:05:01.940 --> 00:05:07.090
At the same time, Chinese chip innovation
is growing by leaps and bounds.

00:05:07.090 --> 00:05:12.370
In 2020, Chinese firms were still struggling
to get below 40 nanometers.

00:05:12.370 --> 00:05:18.330
Today, leading Chinese chip company SMIC is
said to have successfully made a 7-nanometer

00:05:18.330 --> 00:05:19.330
chip.

00:05:19.330 --> 00:05:23.800
Researchers at a firm called TechInsights
say the chip was made for crypto mining.

00:05:23.800 --> 00:05:28.610
China has made it a strategic priority to
boost its domestic semiconductor industry,

00:05:28.610 --> 00:05:33.530
showering Chinese chip firms with incentives,
including exempting them from paying corporate

00:05:33.530 --> 00:05:38.130
income tax for ten years if they make the
most sophisticated chips.

00:05:38.130 --> 00:05:44.009
Still, for now, Taiwan Semiconductor is the
most important chip manufacturer in the world.

00:05:44.009 --> 00:05:49.339
It’s producing chips that are 2 nanometers
smaller than China and vows to start manufacturing

00:05:49.339 --> 00:05:53.460
ultra-advanced 2-nanometer chips by 2025.

00:05:53.460 --> 00:05:57.699
That means your iPhone would last four days
without needing a charge.

00:05:57.699 --> 00:06:02.030
China needs TSMC just as much as the United
States does.

00:06:02.030 --> 00:06:08.370
As geopolitical tensions rise, Taiwan Semiconductors'
importance on the world stage may be the island’s

00:06:08.370 --> 00:06:13.409
greatest protection against any possible invasion.

